---
import {foundation,href} from '../../data';
import Stack from '../layout/Stack.astro';
import Grid from '../layout/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../library/Card.astro';
import TextInput from '../forms/TextInput.astro';
import Button from '../actions/Button.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../component-docs/CodeBlock.astro';
import './foundations.css';
import '../../styles/component-docs.css';
const {page}=Astro.props as {page:'overview'|'principles'|'colour'|'typography'};
const related=page==='overview'?[['For designers','get-started/for-designers/'],['For developers','get-started/for-developers/'],['Patterns overview','patterns/'],['Usage guidelines','resources/usage-guidelines/']]:page==='principles'?[['Forms pattern','patterns/forms/'],['Interaction principles','foundations/interaction-principles/'],['Accessibility','foundations/accessibility/'],['Usage guidelines','resources/usage-guidelines/']]:page==='colour'?[['Colour tokens','design-tokens/colour/'],['Borders and focus','foundations/borders-and-focus/'],['Feedback pattern','patterns/error-and-success-states/'],['Alert','components/feedback/alert/']]:[['Typography tokens','design-tokens/typography/'],['Form field','components/inputs/form-field/'],['For designers','get-started/for-designers/'],['Developer handoff','resources/developer-handoff/']];
const code=page==='colour'?`.reference-copy {\n  background: var(--samvad-semantic-color-bg-default);\n  color: var(--samvad-semantic-color-text-primary);\n  border-color: var(--samvad-semantic-color-border-default);\n}\n/* The quiet Dark boundary resolves to neutral/800. */`:page==='typography'?`.reference-label {\n  font-size: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-size);\n  line-height: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-line-height);\n  font-weight: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-weight);\n}\n/* Existing field labels: 14/20/600; helper/error copy: body/s 14/22/400. */`:null;
---
<div class="foundation-docs component-docs">
{page==='overview'&&<section id="start-here" class="doc-section"><h2>Choose your starting point.</h2><Grid columns={1} medium={2} wide={2} gap={24}><Card title="Design with the shared language" description="Learn the foundations, choose existing components and describe states and behaviour."><a href={href('get-started/for-designers/')}>Start as a designer</a></Card><Card title="Build with the real sources" description="Use local Astro components and traceable token aliases, then verify the full interaction."><a href={href('get-started/for-developers/')}>Start as a developer</a></Card></Grid><h3>How the documentation fits together</h3><ul class="checklist"><li>Foundations explain approved visual values and why they exist.</li><li><a href={href('design-tokens/')}>Tokens</a> connect source values to semantic roles and component mappings in both themes.</li><li><a href={href('components/actions/button/')}>Components</a> document 49 reusable families; <a href={href('patterns/')}>Patterns</a> coordinate complete small interactions.</li><li><a href={href('resources/developer-handoff/')}>Resources</a> support handoff, contribution and change tracking. There is no published package or automatic Figma/code synchronization.</li></ul></section>}
{page==='principles'&&<section id="in-practice" class="doc-section"><h2>Make the principles observable.</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Clarity: use “Clear filter” to recover no matches; do not make the person guess how to restore content.</li><li>Character: use Geist hierarchy and restrained accents rather than adding a decorative control variant.</li><li>Space: use a 24px Stack gap for related sections, while preserving the existing field’s internal spacing.</li><li>Purposeful colour: an Alert includes a title and marker; error meaning does not depend on red alone.</li><li>Consistency: a composed form imports the real TextInput and shared validation helper instead of a look-alike field.</li><li>Access: failed submission focuses a useful error summary; keyboard recovery returns to the affected field.</li></ul><p><a href={href('patterns/forms/')}>Try these decisions together in the form pattern.</a></p></section>}
{page==='colour'&&<><section id="complete-palette" class="doc-section"><h2>Supporting and feedback ramps</h2><p>All remaining 11-step scales, from the same approved source. Apricot/lime are expressive accents; success/warning/error/info have separate semantic roles. A scale value alone does not guarantee contrast.</p>{['apricot','lime','success','warning','error','info'].map(family=><div class="doc-section"><h3>{family}</h3><div class="palette-ramp">{Object.entries(foundation.colors[family as keyof typeof foundation.colors]).map(([step,hex])=><button class="swatch" data-copy={hex} aria-label={`Copy ${family}/${step}: ${hex}`}><span class="swatch-paint" style={{background:hex}}/><span class="swatch-name">{step}</span><span class="swatch-value">{hex}</span></button>)}</div></div>)}</section><section id="semantic-roles" class="doc-section"><h2>Read colour by role, not hex alone.</h2><div class="semantic-role-sample"><Stack gap={16}><p>Primary text on the default surface. This specimen follows the current theme through Semantic aliases.</p><Button>Existing primary action</Button></Stack></div><p>Quiet boundaries: neutral/200 Light and neutral/800 Dark. Required control boundaries: neutral/500. Actions and focus retain their approved mulberry mappings; accents do not substitute for semantic feedback.</p></section></>}
{page==='typography'&&<section id="approved-mappings" class="doc-section"><h2>Read the final component mappings.</h2><div data-foundation-specimen><TextInput id="typography-field" label="Approved label role" helper="Label 14/20/600. Helper and error text 14/22/400."/></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Field/selection labels use the label role. Helper/error copy uses body/s; do not restore the old 13px helper styling.</li><li>OTP tracking remains an approved .125em functional exception. Badge/Table weight 500 and other non-equivalent line-height mappings remain explicitly deferred.</li><li>Geist is the approved available fallback; Geist Mono supports technical labels. Installed variable-font family names are web delivery adapters, not new typeface choices.</li><li>Noto Sans Devanagari and Telugu are documented fallback references, not bundled web fonts. Script specimens start at body 16/28 with zero tracking; native-language review and shaping/font delivery remain integration responsibilities.</li><li>Use rem against the 16px reference without locking the root size. Preserve text scaling; use platform-appropriate sp/dp adapters rather than treating Figma logical sizes as physical pixels.</li></ul></section>}
<section id="connections" class="doc-section"><h2>Continue with the system.</h2><ul>{related.map(([label,path])=><li><a href={href(path)}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul>{code&&<CodeBlock code={code} language="CSS"/>}</section>
</div>
